  "name": "Ciranda (Pernambuco coastal circle dance)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Circle song-dance of the Pernambuco coast and Zona da Mata Norte, especially Itamaracá island, in which dancers hold hands in a ring and step to the strong beat of the bass drum. A mestre cirandeiro sings the verses and the ring answers with the refrain, accompanied by bass drum (bombo or zabumba), snare drum (caixa), ganzá and maracá. A generic membrane-drum card stands in for the bass drum and a source-unspecified shaker for the ganzá.",
